 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The Spirit, who kept not them under,\nSaw the flame of Death's soul come into\nHimself and set them on fire,\nAnd made his own a son, himself,\nFor life is burned but for fire.\nHark! they hear it now, singing high\nTheir voices through the city streets,\nWith the darkness behind upon\nIts face all confused again.\nOh let us know its spirit then\nThat we knew none in earth before. O\nWhat so sweet a sight below",
